rantee excludes a descendant that leaves the session process group and a process another service starts outside the session job: neither is ended, and the kill does not report it. A POSIX zombie under a PID 1 that never reaps keeps the group nonempty, so the kill raises after the bound. A descendant that denies the kill access to wait on it also makes the kill raise, rather than letting the coordinator continue without knowing whether it ended. Stopping is the need's cannot-proceed case, not a supervision fault: continuing would hand the worktree to the next session beside a writer that may still be live, and nothing can proceed \n1868-acceptance_criteria = \"At a wall deadline, an idle deadline, or a coordinator interruption once the platform's process creation has returned the child, the direct session child and every process still in the session process group on POSIX or session job on Windows have ended before the coordinator continues; if any has not ended within 10 s of the kill, the coordinator stops with an error naming what survived instead of continuing.\"\n1869-priority = \"S\"\n1705:[requirement.SR-227]\n1706-title = \"Where the retention dial is on, adjudication routes retain sessions and reset them only when safe\"\n1707-sn_refs = [\"SN-025\"]\n1708-boundary_refs = [\"B-10\"]\n1709-hat_refs = [\"PERFORMANCE\", \"UNATTENDED-OPS\", \"INTEGRITY-RECOVERABILITY\"]\n1710-requirement = \"Where the declared adjudicator retention dial is above zero, the delivered adjudication content shall manage each retained-class adjudication consistently whether the coordinator or loop starts it: resume the route's active, unheld session in its model runner's resume form; mint and record a session id where the route has no active session; wait a bounded time where its active session is held, then run unretained and state why; record each call like any other; drain the session when its latest request's occupancy reaches the dial or the inputs it judges under change; retire it only when no work it has a stake in is pending, except that at the first keep after a blackout w\n1711-rationale = \"\"\"A DERIVED requirement, and labelled so. SN-025 asks that a configured agent implement toward the vision with no human curating what comes next; it does not name retaining a session, so this obligation arrives through three lenses rather than through the need's text. The performance lens listens for an operating-cost risk left unassessed: a run that spins a fresh adjudicator for every small work item reloads the spine on each call, and the usage record makes that cost visible, while resuming a session by id uses the provider's prompt cache. The unattended-operations lens listens for a silent degrade: a retained session that has filled, judges under changed rules, or is sta","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0352a375-be9f-4836-bcc4-e389f08eec57","uuid":"ae405b7e-c944-4d7a-858c-202930f5be22","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:45:51.820Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"3032:[design.LLR-270]\n3033-sr_refs = [\"SR-227\", \"SR-238\"]\n3034-title = \"The keep operation retains adjudicator sessions through act and record, inert at dial 0\"\n3035-module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/session_keep.py;project-trajectory/scripts/session_service.py;project-trajectory/scripts/session_adapters.py;project-trajectory/scripts/agent_loop.py;project-trajectory/scripts/dispatch.py\"\n3036-code_symbol = \"KeepConfig/keep_config/applies/FAMILY_RESET_CAP/GOVERNING_INPUT_FILES/GOVERNING_INPUT_GLOBS/HOME_VARIABLES/primary_out_dir/store_lock/dir_lock/store_load/write_tombstone/load_honoured/is_lease_only/_apply_tombstone/_drop_lease/store_remove/keep_release/retire_stale_lease/dedicated_home_env/governing_hash/drain_reason/lineage/chain_pending/is_clear_point/retire_after_blackout/keep_for/keep_argv/keep_bookkeep/keep_abandon/keepwarm_due/_prepare_warm/_warm_candidates/_warm_keep/take_warm_lease;cli_version/plan_keep/KeepWarmer/KeepWarmer._raise_unended/_pi