{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfuqv9c4YvxPAuJ16ubB1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ruled both amended rows **MEANING**, and because the LLR and TC rungs are released, I re-attested both myself.\n\n**Verdict** (`7d02eacd9`, trailer `WI: WI-895`, file `docs/reviews/wi-895/001-ADJUDICATE-8f38a13.md`). It has one `## amendment` section ending in `VERDICT: MEANING rows=2`, and the file ends in `SITTING: JUDGED kinds=amendment`.\n- **LLR-270 Detail:** the old text said nothing about a keep-warm ping whose launch fails, so a build that swallowed every ping failure met it. The new text adds a case: a `TreeNotEnded` from the ping now stops the run, raised at the next tick or at the run's end.\n  - Over a clean trunk, the call is recorded first, and a recording failure rides as the exception's context.\n  - Over a dirty trunk, it is raised without being recorded, and the dirty-trunk hold does not delay it.\n  - Every other ping failure is recorded as an ERROR and the run continues. That rule is also newly stated.\n- **TC-268 Method:** it now owes four checks it didn't owe before. A run of the old method could pass with none of them.\n\n**Why I'd bless both:**\n- **Upward:** the new clause is what SR-238's acceptance asks for, \"stops with an error ... instead of continuing\". The keep-warm ping was the last caller swallowing that stop. LLR-270 now names SR-238 as a parent; the anchor had only SR-227. The ERROR-and-continue rule keeps SR-227's \"record each call like any other\".\n- **Closed obligation:** the actor, the trigger, both trunk states, the run's end and the exemption for other failures are all stated and observable.\n- **Downward:** TC-268's Evidence names one test per new arm. I ran those four plus the related keep-warm tests in `tests/test_session_keep.py`: **10 passed, 67 deselected**.\n\n**Re-attestation** (`87689d2dd`, separate commit). I ran `python project-trajectory/scripts/intake.py --root . snapshot --reattests LLR-270,TC-268`, which recorded act 106. Nothing was refused, and both anchor copies now match the live registries byte for byte. The copy takes the whole file, so it also picked up LLR-298's and LLR-302's `module` and `code_symbol` cells from WI-892's move on trunk. Those are trace cells only, and no other row's normative text moved; I said so in the commit message.\n\nBoth commits passed their checks (`RESULT: PASS`). The checks also reported two readability worsenings from the lane's code, neither in a gating measure. I edited no registry cell. The untracked `.requested` marker is still there."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1982,"cache_read_input_tokens":164135,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1982},"output_tokens":772,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0352a375-be9f-4836-bcc4-e389f08eec57","uuid":"879607d2-e054-4825-98c6-411c848573f3","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:47:55.465Z","request_id":"req_011Cfuqv93prAuR5nnCRRW72"}
